[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to the use of a static or predictable initialization vector (IV) in the AES or DES encryption process when using CBC mode. This vulnerability occurs because the code does not specify that a unique, randomly generated IV should be used for each encryption operation. Using a static or predictable IV can compromise the security of the encrypted data by allowing attackers to deduce information about the plaintext or recover the encryption key through known-plaintext attacks.

